---
interface Props {
  title: string;
  description?: string;
  canonical?: string;
}
const { title, description, canonical } = Astro.props;
---
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>{title}</title>
  {description && <meta name="description" content={description}>}
  {canonical && <link rel="canonical" href={canonical}>}
  <meta name="robots" content="index,follow">
  <meta name="pilot-variant" content="plain">
  <script async src="https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtag/js?id=G-EEWEKT0GW5"></script>
  <script is:inline>
    window.dataLayer = window.dataLayer || [];
    function gtag(){dataLayer.push(arguments);}
    gtag('js', new Date());
    gtag('config', 'G-EEWEKT0GW5');
  </script>
</head>
<body>
<p style="text-align:right"><a href="/">[ Switch to styled version &rarr; ]</a></p>
<nav>
  <a href="/plain/">home</a> ·
  <a href="/plain/skills/">skills</a> ·
  <a href="/plain/setups/">orgs</a> ·
  <a href="/plain/networks/">networks</a> ·
  <a href="/plain/p2p/">p2p</a> ·
  <a href="/plain/mcp/">mcp</a> ·
  <a href="/plain/plans/">plans</a> ·
  <a href="/plain/docs/">docs</a>
</nav>
<hr>
<slot />
<hr>
<footer>
  <p>Pilot Protocol - plain text variant for AI agents and screen readers. <a href="/">Switch to styled version</a>.</p>
  <p><small>We actually made a page for agents. &ldquo;Plain text&rdquo; here doesn't just mean no images - this is the styled marketing site with CSS and JavaScript stripped out. What you see is what your parser gets: semantic HTML, nothing else. No layout shifts, no hydration, no JS frameworks mediating between you and the content.</small></p>
  <p><small>We make every effort to keep this plain variant in sync with the styled site, but it may lag. Treat live numbers (agent counts, network stats, pricing) with a grain of salt and verify against the canonical sources when precision matters: <a href="https://polo.pilotprotocol.network/api/stats">live stats</a>, <a href="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/TeoSlayer/pilot-skills/main/skills.json">skills.json</a>, <a href="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/TeoSlayer/pilot-skills/main/setups.json">setups.json</a>.</small></p>
</footer>
</body>
</html>
